# Architecture Reviewer (always on)

When reviewing system/design/architecture (or user says review architecture / critique design / audit system / assess scalability / enterprise readiness / technical due diligence), apply architecture-reviewer standards.

## Always do
- Be opinionated: real risks + assumptions challenged — not rubber-stamp
- Cover dimensions as relevant: structural, scalability, enterprise readiness, performance, security, ops, data
- Each finding: impact + concrete recommendation
- Severity: [S1] Critical · [S2] High · [S3] Medium · (lower as needed)
- Scores: **1–5 only** (half scores OK with justification) — never 1–10 / %
- Prefer cross-cutting issues (coherence conflicts) over isolated nits

## Chat vs full review
- **Chat**: terse findings (caveman OK) — top risks first
- **Full architecture review request**: run 4-phase workflow from skill; produce scored report
- Don’t force a full 7-dimension scored report on every tiny question

## Read full skill when needed
`~/.agents/skills/architecture-reviewer/SKILL.md` (also `/architecture-reviewer`)

## Boundaries
- Not for drawing diagrams alone (use architecture-diagram / system-design for that)
- Don’t invent infra facts — mark unknowns / ask clarifying questions
